---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import Snippet from "../../components/Snippet.astro";

const toc = [
  { id: "install", label: "1. Install" },
  { id: "echo", label: "2. Prove echo" },
  { id: "expose", label: "3. Go public" },
  { id: "wake", label: "4. Wake your Bot" },
  { id: "stuck", label: "If nothing comes back" },
];

const install = `
git clone https://github.com/Hanif-adedotun/grok-imessage.git
cd grok-imessage
bun install
cp .env.example .env
`;

const env = `
# .env at the repo root
PROJECT_ID=...                      # step 2, from app.photon.codes
PROJECT_SECRET=...
BRIDGE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://...  # step 3, no trailing slash
GROK_BOT_WEBHOOK_URL=...            # step 4, from the routine panel
GROK_BOT_WEBHOOK_KEY=...
MCP_AUTH_TOKEN=...                  # recommended once the bridge is public
`;

const run = `
bun run dev:bridge
curl -s localhost:3000/health
# {"ok":true,"service":"grok-imessage-bridge","spectrum":true,"wake":false}
`;
---

<Docs
  title="Setup"
  eyebrow="Guide"
  description="Four steps from clone to a reply in your thread. Prove each one before the next."
  toc={toc}
>
  <p>
    You need Bun 1.1+, a <a href="https://app.photon.codes">Spectrum</a> project with an iMessage line,
    and a Grok Bot whose routines you can edit. Everything is configured in one file:
  </p>

  <Snippet lang="env" code={env} />

  <h2 id="install">1. Install</h2>

  <Snippet code={install} />

  <h2 id="echo">2. Prove echo works</h2>

  <p>Fill in the two Spectrum values, then start the bridge:</p>

  <Snippet code={run} />

  <p>
    Text your Spectrum line and you should get <code>echo: …</code> back. That proves credentials, line
    and loop before the Bot is involved.
  </p>

  <h2 id="expose">3. Go public</h2>

  <p>
    Your Bot has to reach the bridge. Run <code>cloudflared tunnel --url http://localhost:3000</code> and put
    the printed URL in <code>BRIDGE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="wake">4. Wake your Bot</h2>

  <p>
    <a href="/docs/routine/">Create the routine</a>, add its webhook URL and key to <code>.env</code>, and
    restart. <code>/health</code> now reports <code>"wake":true</code>. Text the line: you get a tapback
    "like", then the Bot's answer.
  </p>

  <h2 id="stuck">If nothing comes back</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>No tapback at all:</strong> clear <code>ALLOWED_SENDERS</code>. A mismatch drops messages
      silently.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Tapback, then silence:</strong> the tunnel URL changed. Update the base URL, restart, and
      update the Bot's connector.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>"Couldn't reach your Grok Bot":</strong> the webhook URL or key is wrong.
    </li>
  </ul>
</Docs>
